From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: OHPC <ohpc@example.com>
Date: Wed, 1 Oct 2026 22:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] cmake: decouple tools/examples from EVMC_TESTING and allow
 dependency discovery without Hunter

Two upstream CMake issues prevent the complete EVMC build (libraries + tools +
examples + the full CTest suite) in the offline OpenHarmony cross-build.

1) Hunter is used to obtain the build/test-time dependencies (GTest for the
   internal unit tests and the evmc-vmtester tool, CLI11 for the evmc-tool
   CLI). Hunter is a network-only package manager: on the first configure it
   downloads and bootstraps an archive from GitHub, which cannot work offline.
   HunterGate.cmake already implements a "disabled mode" -- with
   HUNTER_ENABLED=OFF the HunterGate() macro installs an empty
   hunter_add_package() and skips all network access. The obstacle is that the
   upstream CMakeLists includes HunterGate.cmake and calls HunterGate()
   exclusively inside `if(HUNTER_ENABLED)`, so with HUNTER_ENABLED=OFF the macro
   is never evaluated and hunter_add_package stays undefined at its use sites
   in test/unittests/CMakeLists.txt, tools/vmtester/CMakeLists.txt and
   tools/evmc/CMakeLists.txt.

   Fix: always include HunterGate.cmake and always call HunterGate(). With
   HUNTER_ENABLED=ON this is behaviour-preserving (the gate is a no-op after
   the first call). With HUNTER_ENABLED=OFF it enables Hunter's documented
   disabled mode and the dependencies are resolved by find_package() against
   the ambient CMake package registry (here: Conan's CMakeDeps packages).

2) EVMC_TOOLS and EVMC_EXAMPLES were declared with cmake_dependent_option()
   guarded by "NOT EVMC_TESTING" and <force> = ON. CMakeDependentOption sets
   the option to <force> whenever the dependency is false
   (CMakeDependentOption.cmake: `set(${option} ${force})`), so with
   EVMC_TESTING=ON -- exactly when the test suite is requested -- both options
   were forced ON regardless of any -D on the command line, and could not be
   turned off. The forced EVMC_TOOLS also feeds HUNTER_ENABLED's default
   (`${EVMC_TOOLS}`), which re-enables Hunter's network bootstrap, and pulls in
   tools/, whose evmc-vmtester target test/vmtester/CMakeLists.txt requires
   (evmc_add_vm_test() raises FATAL_ERROR without it).

   Fix: declare both as plain options with the same OFF defaults, so the caller
   can actually choose. With EVMC_TESTING=OFF nothing changes (both default to
   OFF, so a plain library-only build is identical to before).

No test case, assertion, test input or expected exit code is modified.
diff --git a/CMakeLists.txt b/CMakeLists.txt
index e2344af..fb61c4a 100644
--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -20,18 +20,33 @@ option(EVMC_INSTALL "Enable EVMC installation (e.g. make install)" ON)
 
 option(EVMC_TESTING "Build everything (libraries, tools, examples, internal tests)" OFF)
 
-cmake_dependent_option(EVMC_TOOLS "Build EVMC tools" OFF
-    "NOT EVMC_TESTING" ON)
-
-cmake_dependent_option(EVMC_EXAMPLES "Build EVMC examples" OFF
-    "NOT EVMC_TESTING" ON)
+# These are plain options rather than cmake_dependent_options on
+# EVMC_TESTING. CMakeDependentOption resolves the option to <force> (=ON here)
+# whenever the dependency is false, so with EVMC_TESTING=ON both were forced ON
+# and could not be turned off from the command line; the forced EVMC_TOOLS also
+# feeds HUNTER_ENABLED's default and re-enables Hunter's network bootstrap.
+option(EVMC_TOOLS "Build EVMC tools" OFF)
+option(EVMC_EXAMPLES "Build EVMC examples" OFF)
 
 option(HUNTER_ENABLED "Enable Hunter package manager support" ${EVMC_TOOLS})
 
+# HunterGate.cmake must be included and HunterGate() called unconditionally.
+# With HUNTER_ENABLED=ON this is behaviour-preserving (the gate is a no-op after
+# the first call, and this is exactly where upstream called it). With
+# HUNTER_ENABLED=OFF it installs a no-op hunter_add_package() -- Hunter's
+# documented "disabled mode" -- so the dependencies can be resolved by
+# find_package() against the ambient CMake package registry (here: Conan's
+# CMakeDeps output) instead of being bootstrapped over the network.
+include(HunterGate)
+
+HunterGate(
+    URL "https://github.com/cpp-pm/hunter/archive/v0.25.6.tar.gz"
+    SHA1 "69e4a05bd514bb05cb2c5aa02ce8ac420516aaf7"
+)
+
 if(HUNTER_ENABLED)
     set(HUNTER_CONFIGURATION_TYPES Release CACHE STRING "Build type of Hunter packages")
     option(HUNTER_USE_CACHE_SERVERS "Use default Hunter cache servers" NO)
-    include(HunterGate)
     include(Hunter/init)
 endif()
 
